IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sgia-p5-penal-court`

-- Tests for sgia-p5-penal-court.l4 (ss 38 to 41E). Expected values are written from the text of each section;
-- the three tables are tested row by row, both ways where the Act has both columns.

§ `ss 38 to 41`

#ASSERT `an attempt to commit the offence is an offence against the provision, punishable as if the offence itself had been committed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an attempt to commit the offence is an offence against the provision, punishable as if the offence itself had been committed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an attempt to commit the offence is an offence against the provision, punishable as if the offence itself had been committed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty relieves the person from liability to answer for damages to a person injured` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the penalty relieves the person from liability to answer for damages to a person injured` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty relieves the person from liability to answer for damages to a person injured` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 40: an act or omission that is an offence under 2 or more written laws (1 law is outside the section)
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under any one of those written laws` 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under any one of those written laws` 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under any one of those written laws` 1 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under any one of those written laws` 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same offence` 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same offence` 1 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same offence` 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 41: the penalty provided is a maximum
#ASSERT `the most the offence is punishable by on conviction` 2000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `the most the offence is punishable by on conviction` 2000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty imposed is within what section 41 allows` 2000 2000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the penalty imposed is within what section 41 allows` 1999 2000 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the penalty imposed is within what section 41 allows` 2001 2000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the penalty imposed is within what section 41 allows` 2001 2000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 41A: process for making applications to Court in civil proceedings`

-- (c): an application that commences the proceedings, made on or after 1 April 2022, where the law prescribes no process
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 4 2022) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `an originating application`
-- the day before 1 April 2022 is outside
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 31 3 2022) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): the law prescribes a petition, motion, originating motion or summons in chambers
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `an originating application`
-- (d): made in proceedings that are pending: a summons
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `a summons`
-- the law prescribes some other process: s 41A(1) does not reach it
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): petitions of appeal, and classes prescribed under (7), are excluded
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` FALSE (Date 1 6 2023) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- neither commencing nor pending: the Act does not say
#ASSERT `the process the application must be made by` TRUE (Date 1 6 2023) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `that provision has any effect in relation to the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `that provision has any effect in relation to the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `that provision has any effect in relation to the application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the application must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the application must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Court may give the parties directions the Court thinks just and expedient to facilitate the progress of the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Court may give the parties directions the Court thinks just and expedient to facilitate the progress of the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`section 41A prevents the relief being included among the reliefs sought in an originating claim` TRUE)
-- (5): made before 1 April 2022 and pending on or after it: the old practice continues, unless the Court orders otherwise
#ASSERT `the application continues under the practice and procedure in force immediately before 1 April 2022` TRUE (Date 31 3 2022) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the application continues under the practice and procedure in force immediately before 1 April 2022` TRUE (Date 31 3 2022) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the application continues under the practice and procedure in force immediately before 1 April 2022` TRUE (Date 1 4 2022) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the application continues under the practice and procedure in force immediately before 1 April 2022` TRUE (Date 31 3 2022) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the application continues under the practice and procedure in force immediately before 1 April 2022` FALSE (Date 31 3 2022) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `the Court of Appeal or a judge sitting in that Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `the Appellate Division of the High Court or a judge sitting in that Division` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `the General Division of the High Court or a judge sitting in that Division` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `a District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `a Magistrate's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `another court prescribed under section 41A(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is a Court for section 41A` `some other court` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 41B: renaming of prerogative orders or writs (as from 1 January 2006)`

#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "mandamus" (Date 1 1 2006) EQUALS JUST "Mandatory Order"
#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "certiorari" (Date 1 1 2006) EQUALS JUST "Quashing Order"
#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "prohibition" (Date 1 1 2006) EQUALS JUST "Prohibiting Order"
#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "writ of habeas corpus" (Date 1 1 2006) EQUALS JUST "Order for Review of Detention"
#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "mandamus" (Date 31 12 2005) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "mandamus" (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST "Mandatory Order"
#ASSERT `the prerogative order or writ issuable by the High Court is referred to as` "injunction" (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT count `the table of section 41B` EQUALS 4

§ `s 41C: references to the High Court in written laws enacted or made before 2 January 2021`

#ASSERT `the reference to the High Court is read as` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 2 1 2021) `a provision conferring jurisdiction or power on the High Court` EQUALS JUST "conferring that jurisdiction or power on the General Division of the High Court"
#ASSERT `the reference to the High Court is read as` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 2 1 2021) `an appeal or other process to or from the High Court` EQUALS JUST "an appeal to or from the General Division of the High Court"
#ASSERT `the reference to the High Court is read as` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 2 1 2021) `a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to proceedings in the High Court` EQUALS JUST "a power to make subsidiary legislation in relation to proceedings in both the General Division of the High Court and Appellate Division of the High Court"
-- boundaries: the law must pre-date 2 January 2021, and the reading must be on or after it
#ASSERT `the reference to the High Court is read as` (Date 2 1 2021) (Date 2 1 2021) `an appeal or other process to or from the High Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference to the High Court is read as` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 2 1 2021) `an appeal or other process to or from the High Court` EQUALS JUST "an appeal to or from the General Division of the High Court"
#ASSERT `the reference to the High Court is read as` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 1 1 2021) `an appeal or other process to or from the High Court` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 41D(1): references to writs, etc. (as from 1 April 2022)`

#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Originating claim"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Originating summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Originating application"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Subpoena" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Order to attend court"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of execution" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Enforcement order"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of seizure and sale" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Enforcement order for seizure and sale of property"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of possession" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Enforcement order for possession of property"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Garnishee order" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Enforcement order for attachment of a debt"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Memorandum of appearance" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Notice of intention to contest or not contest"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Entry of appearance in relation to a writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Filing and service of a notice of intention to contest or not contest"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Leave of court" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Permission of court"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Plaintiff" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Claimant"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Ex parte application" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Application without notice"
#ASSERT count `the table of section 41D(1)` EQUALS 12
-- the day before 1 April 2022
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Plaintiff" (Date 31 3 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a second-column expression is not translated again outside the family exception
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Claimant" (Date 1 1 2023) `any other proceedings` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41D(3) is deleted` EQUALS "(3) [Deleted by Act 19 of 2025 wef 05/12/2025]"

§ `s 41D(2): proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division, a Family Court or a Youth Court`

#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Originating claim" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Writ of summons"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Originating application" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Originating summons"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Order to attend court" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Subpoena"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Enforcement order" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Writ of execution"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Enforcement order for seizure and sale of property" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Writ of seizure and sale"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Enforcement order for possession of property" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Writ of possession"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Enforcement order for attachment of a debt" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Garnishee order"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Notice of intention to contest or not contest" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Memorandum of appearance"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Filing and service of a notice of intention to contest or not contest" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Entry of appearance in relation to a writ of summons"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Permission of court" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Leave of court"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Claimant" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Plaintiff"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Application without notice" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Ex parte application"
-- a first-column reference in the same proceedings follows s 41D(1)
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Plaintiff" (Date 1 1 2024) `proceedings commenced before 15 October 2024 in the Family Division of the High Court, a Family Court or a Youth Court` EQUALS JUST "Claimant"

§ `s 41E: the Singapore International Commercial Court (as from 1 April 2022)`

#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Originating claim" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Originating application"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Originating application"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Notice of intention to contest or not contest" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Defendant's statement"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Memorandum of appearance" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Defendant's statement"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Filing and service of a notice of intention to contest or not contest" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Filing and service of a defendant's statement"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Entry of appearance in relation to a writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Filing and service of a defendant's statement"
#ASSERT count `the table of section 41E` EQUALS 6
-- "Writ of summons" is "Originating claim" under s 41D(1) but "Originating application" for the Singapore International Commercial Court
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `any other proceedings` EQUALS JUST "Originating claim"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Originating application"
-- a matter s 41E does not list: s 41D(1) still applies (fork F18)
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Subpoena" (Date 1 4 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS JUST "Order to attend court"
#ASSERT `the reference is construed as a reference to` "Writ of summons" (Date 31 3 2022) `proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court` EQUALS NOTHING
